<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="hero-service">
<div class="container">
<h2>Backup &amp; Disaster Recovery</h2>
<p>Protect your business from data loss, hardware failure and unexpected outages.</p>
</div>
</section>

<main class="container">

<div class="service-block">
<h3>What this service includes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Local and cloud backup design and setup</li>
<li>Automated backup scheduling</li>
<li>Recovery testing and verification</li>
<li>Business continuity planning</li>
<li>Secure storage configuration</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="service-block">
<h3>Who this is for</h3>
<p>Any business that relies on critical data, applications or systems to operate.</p>
</div>

<div class="service-block">
<h3>Problems this solves</h3>
<ul>
<li>Permanent data loss after incidents</li>
<li>Ransomware impact with no recovery path</li>
<li>Hardware failure with no backups</li>
<li>Accidental deletion of important files</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="service-block">
<h3>How the service works</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Data audit:</strong> Identify critical systems, data and recovery objectives.</li>
<li><strong>Backup design:</strong> Choose appropriate local and cloud solutions.</li>
<li><strong>Implementation:</strong> Configure backups and monitoring.</li>
<li><strong>Recovery testing:</strong> Prove that restore works before you need it.</li>
</ol>
</div>

<div class="service-block">
<h3>Get started</h3>
<p>Put a realistic, tested recovery plan in place before you need it.</p>
<p><a class="button" href="/#contact">Review your backup strategy</a></p>
</div>

</main>

<!-- FAQ SECTION -->
<section class="service-block">
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <h3>How often should backups be tested?</h3>
  <p>We recommend quarterly restore tests to ensure your data can be recovered reliably.</p>

  <h3>Do you support hybrid backup setups?</h3>
  <p>Yes — we design solutions combining local storage and cloud backup for maximum resilience.</p>

  <h3>Can you recover data after ransomware?</h3>
  <p>If backups exist, recovery is usually possible. We ensure you always have a clean restore point.</p>

  <h3>Do you monitor backup success?</h3>
  <p>Yes — automated monitoring alerts us to failures so issues can be fixed before they become critical.</p>
</section>

